// Ch9 B03-B08: the gilt line, the Ebbing in three movements and the cutaway, then "Pointing the wrong
// way" (docs/kb/story/beats/act1_ch09.md §2 B03-B08, §7 shots). ONE scene with a node per beat, so every
// cut between beats is a cut (separate scenes would hand the camera back to the field between them).
// THE RULES (§0): every mote is HELD (glimmer_held, cyan) and drifts DOWN and SEAWARD; nothing rises or
// turns gold; no release anywhere. Nothing interrupts the Ebbing: no spawn, no battle, no alarm.
// THE HELD INPUT (§2 B04-B07; §9 UI 1): each movement runs between <<event hold_input raise_staff>> and
// <<event hold_input_end>>. In between, the scene's time runs only while the player holds the field's
// interact action ("Hold to raise the staff": CutsceneHoldGate, game/data/flow/ch09_field.json). No
// timing, no score, no fail: let go and the dance waits, breathing. The player is not performing the
// dance; they are letting it go on. The full Ebbing render (staff and mourner attractors, thousands of
// motes, the reflection, the absorption bloom) is Rendering's (M3-C09-03); the @vfx here are the
// placeholder held motes.
title: ch09_the_ebbing
location: ch09/corrow_night
---
// B03 "The gilt line" (E, 1.5 min). N06: CU, the Tender's brush painting the gilt line on Asha's face
// (N-04: "so the dead can find her"), its first appearance in the game. Asha holds still, eyes shut.
// Ysolde's warmth comes out as an instruction, played sincerely (in hindsight it is the instruction for
// leading the dead the wrong way). N07: Asha steps onto the raft alone; the strand kneels facing the
// water. Rhen kneels at the waterline if he sat with his own dead at Haluna, else at the back of the
// strand. Pell is not in the frame.
@letterbox on
@anim asha stand_gilt
@camera N06
@music corrow_night fade=1.0
@anim tender paint_gilt asha
@wait 2.5
@mark ysolde ysolde_landing walk
@wait 1.0
Ysolde [tender]: Keep the lamp above your shoulder, not your head. They follow the light, not you. Let them. #line:ch09_gilt_001
@wait 1.0
@camera N07
@mark asha raft_step walk
@mark toma strand_toma walk
<<if $ch02_rhen_stayed_with_dead>>
    @mark rhen kneel_waterline walk
<<else>>
    @mark rhen kneel_back walk
<<endif>>
@sfx shingle_kneel
@music silence fade=2.0
@wait 3.0
<<jump ch09_ebb_gathering>>
===
// B04, first movement, "the gathering" (C -> E, 2 min). N08 (24 mm, high, from the strand): the raft
// small on the black harbour, the broken wall behind, the motes hanging over the low town. Asha raises
// the staff (input 1). The motes come up off the low town's still water, over the broken wall, and OFF
// THE MOURNERS, leaving them reluctantly. N09: a mourner's open hand on the shingle, the motes lifting
// off her fingers (lifting off, not rising up: they stay low). N10: Asha's face, the gilt line catching
// the lantern, eyes on the light.
title: ch09_ebb_gathering
---
@camera N08
@anim asha pole_out
@sfx raft_pole
@vfx glimmer_held at=lowtown_motes count=24 drift=down_seaward rate=slow
@wait 2.0
<<event hold_input raise_staff>>
@music the_ebbing fade=3.0
@anim asha raise_staff
@sfx staff_bell_shells
@vfx glimmer_held at=mourners_motes count=18 drift=down_seaward rate=slow
@wait 6.0
@camera N09
@vfx glimmer_held at=mourner_hand count=8 drift=down_seaward rate=slow
@wait 3.0
@camera N10
@wait 3.0
<<event hold_input_end>>
<<jump ch09_ebb_long_line>>
===
// B05, second movement, "the long line" (E, 1.5 min). Input 2. N11, the hero frame (18 mm, low over
// the water; motes may bloom to 35% of the frame, and this is that frame): thousands of motes stream
// after the staff in a long curving river of cyan across the harbour, reflected in the still water.
// Asha turns on the raft, and the river turns with her. N11 holds at least 6 s with the input. N12
// (24 mm, from the water's surface looking up): the stream passing overhead and SINKING as it goes.
title: ch09_ebb_long_line
---
<<event hold_input raise_staff>>
@camera N11
@anim asha turn_on_raft
@sfx staff_bell_shells
@vfx glimmer_held at=harbour_stream count=36 drift=down_seaward rate=normal
@wait 7.0
@camera N12
@vfx glimmer_held at=stream_overhead count=24 drift=down_seaward rate=normal
@wait 4.0
<<event hold_input_end>>
<<jump ch09_the_stair>>
===
// B06, cutaway: the stair (C, 15 s). N13, ONE SHOT, cut in and cut out (ADR 0022 (f) and its sweep-G
// S4 note; rule 2): the landward side of the wall, the Fisher Stair rising out of the drowned low town
// at slack water. A big man in a straw cape, ALONE, carrying a child's body up the stair (wrapped in
// sailcloth, face covered), climbing slowly; low wide, his back three-quarters to us, a silhouette,
// never a face close-up. Over the wall-head behind and above him the river of motes passes seaward and
// down, AWAY from him. No other figure on the stair. NO MOTE TURNS TOWARD HIM (that is Ch15's). NO
// ROPE-BURN GLOW (it starts in Ch10). The music is the Ebbing's, muffled by the wall (Audio's mix).
// Not a held input: the dance is elsewhere. Nobody in the party ever mentions it.
title: ch09_the_stair
---
@camera N13
@vfx glimmer_held at=wallhead_motes count=24 drift=down_seaward rate=normal
@mark kerrid_stair stair_climb walk
@wait 15.0
<<jump ch09_ebb_letting_down>>
===
// B07, third movement, "letting down" (E -> C, 1.5 min). Input 3. N14 (50 mm, from the raft's side):
// Asha lowers the staff toward the harbour mouth, and the river of light goes out between the moles
// toward open sea and SINKS, absorbed into the sea's own faint glow. N15 (35 mm, wide): the harbour dark
// again, the sea-glow a little brighter than before, Asha alone on the raft with the lantern. It is
// done, and it is lovely, and it is wrong.
title: ch09_ebb_letting_down
---
<<event hold_input raise_staff>>
@camera N14
@anim asha lower_staff
@sfx staff_bell_shells
@vfx glimmer_held at=harbour_mouth count=36 drift=down_seaward rate=slow
@wait 6.0
<<event hold_input_end>>
@camera N15
@music silence fade=3.0
@sfx harbour_lap
@wait 4.0
<<set $ch09_ebbing_danced = true>>
<<jump ch09_wrong_way>>
===
// B08 "Pointing the wrong way" (C, 3 min, ~110 words). N16: the raft comes in; Asha steps off radiant
// and spent, the gilt line streaked with spray; Rhen is first to her. Her quiet line is for him alone
// (asha_velamir.md's private notice; paid off in Ch10). N17: a very tall shape has come down the rocks
// at the strand's end, the Kirru from the wall (2.3 m: shoot low on him). Toma's hand goes to his spear
// and stays there. Pell stands still for a long time, the way the Kirru do, then speaks HIS FIRST WORDS
// IN THE GAME (rule 6; mandated text, one line: the long gap after "Beautiful." is VO timing, see the
// line's note). He doesn't explain, and he doesn't answer Asha's question (Ch10's farewell-tide does).
// N18: Toma, who has spent the night among his own dead, gives Pell the words he gave Rhen on Haluna's
// dock in Ch3: a man too tired to refuse, and kinder than his creed. N19: if the party fed the beacon in
// Ch8, Fenn tells Asha her mother danced for Corrow's drowned (ADR 0022 (a)); otherwise Hobb, unprompted.
// Kerrid is absent: he has no line here.
title: ch09_wrong_way
---
@fade out 1.0
@anim asha pole_in
@camera N16
@music corrow_night fade=4.0
@fade in 1.0
@mark rhen landing_rhen walk
@wait 1.5
Asha [exhausted]: Was it all right? From the shore? #line:ch09_wrong_way_001
Rhen [tender]: It was the most— Yeah. It was. #line:ch09_wrong_way_002
@wait 1.0
Asha [worried]: They didn't want to go, Rhen. I had to keep asking them. #line:ch09_wrong_way_003 #whisper
<<set $ch09_asha_said_they_hung_back = true>>
@wait 1.5
@camera N17
@mark pell rocks_foot walk via=way_rocks_top,way_rocks_down,way_rocks_turn
@wait 3.0
@anim toma hand_on_spear
@wait 2.5
Pell [neutral]: Beautiful. And pointing the wrong way. #line:ch09_wrong_way_004 #tn:"Pell's first words in the game. A long silence after 'Beautiful.' (at least 1.5 s), then the rest. He is not sneering."
@wait 1.5
Ysolde [cold]: The rite has been danced the same way for nine hundred years. #line:ch09_wrong_way_005
Pell [neutral]: Yes. #line:ch09_wrong_way_006
@wait 1.5
Asha [worried]: Which way should they point? #line:ch09_wrong_way_007
@wait 2.5
Pell [neutral]: You go where it sleeps. #line:ch09_wrong_way_008
Asha [neutral]: The Choir. Yes. #line:ch09_wrong_way_009
Pell [neutral]: I will walk there too. #line:ch09_wrong_way_010
Rhen [worried]: Who are you? #line:ch09_wrong_way_011
@wait 2.0
@camera N18
@anim toma look_at pell
@wait 2.5
Toma [exhausted]: ...Walk behind me, then. #line:ch09_wrong_way_012
Asha [tender]: Thank you, Toma. #line:ch09_wrong_way_013
<<set $ch09_pell_joined = true>>
@camera N19
<<if $ch08_fed_the_beacon>>
    @mark fenn fenn_up walk
    @wait 1.5
    Fenn [tender]: Your mother danced for our drowned too. Same harbour. #line:ch09_wrong_way_014
<<else>>
    @mark hobb hobb_up walk
    @wait 1.5
    Hobb [neutral]: The last Cantor danced it for us, the year of the last Rising. You did it well. #line:ch09_wrong_way_015
<<endif>>
@anim asha look_at harbour_mouth
@wait 2.5
@fade out 2.5
===
